  [1mAntigravity (Gemini 3.8 Flash High)[0m
  For a single-node demo application, [1mSQLite[0m is typically the optimal choice to minimize setup friction and
  operational overhead:
  - [1mZero configuration:[0m It runs in-process with zero external dependencies, making your demo instantly
    portable and trivial to reset or clone from a single file.
  - [1mSufficient capability:[0m It offers full ACID compliance and robust performance that easily surpasses typical
    demonstration workloads without consuming background system resources.
  - [1mWhen to use Postgres:[0m Opt for Postgres only if the demo explicitly showcases engine-specific features,
    such as [38;5;153mpgvector[39m, [38;5;153mLISTEN[39m/[38;5;153mNOTIFY[39m, or advanced concurrency models.

  [1mCodex (gpt-6-astra)[0m
  - [1mUse SQLite, Alex[0m: a single-node demo benefits from simple setup, local storage, and no separate database
    service to manage. [94m]8;id=1mumutq;https://www.sqlite.org/whentouse.html\SQLite guidance[39m]8;;\
  - Choose [1mPostgres[0m if the demo needs Postgres-specific features or must reproduce an existing Postgres
    production environment.
  - Otherwise, start with SQLite and spend the saved setup time on the demo itself.

